      "note": "PROVISIONAL machine alignment reconciled by Codex from independent Tibetan-first and English-first proposals. brgya pa is an abbreviated work title attested here as 400 Verses, not a numeral gloss of brgya. sogs owns the established closing gesture and such, including its connective. The positive premise rtog pa yod pa kho nas yod pa nyid dang is not separately rendered by the negative-only English commentary clause and is omitted. The later rtog pa med par is retained whole so its conceptions cannot attach to the omitted earlier positive occurrence. Complete existential negatives remain at phrase depth. thag pa bsdogs pa is the compositional phrase coil of rope; the supplied you is unwrapped. The two rang gi ngo bos units retain their instrumental and reflexive relation to essence; their essence members are literal. The last definition is not banked whole: de la bltos te has a dependency and referent not securely rendered by through the process of conceptualization, and the English things subject cannot be read back into the Tibetan conception predicate. Only the locally secure Conception and occur atoms are retained; this does not endorse the entire relation. C16:808 differs in English vocabulary; P7:9 ends before the last word and ILL:1109 does not translate the closing definitions. Neither supports the unquoted closing relation or proves publication lineage."
